  "question": "If $\\vec{a} = 2 \\vec{i} + \\vec{j} - 3\\vec{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = \\lambda \\vec{i} + 2\\vec{j} + \\vec{k}$ are perpendicular vectors, find the value of $\\lambda$.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Given: $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are perpendicular, so $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$<br /><br />$\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = (2)(\\lambda) + (1)(2) + (-3)(1)$<br /><br />$= 2\\lambda + 2 - 3$<br /><br />$= 2\\lambda - 1 = 0$<br /><br />$\\implies 2\\lambda = 1$<br /><br />$\\boxed{\\lambda = \\dfrac{1}{2}}$",
